// gradient.okl — Conserved-variable gradient at quadrature points.
//
// RESERVED SKELETON. The viscous path of the DG field module requires the
// gradients of the conserved variables at the quadrature points before the
// viscous flux can be evaluated (see docs/tech_docs/
// governed_equations_and_DG_field.md, Section (二), "粘性项处理").
//
// The future kernel computes, per element and per quadrature point,
//
//   [ dq/dx ; dq/dy ] = J^-T * [ sum_m u[m] * dV2D_r[q][m] ;
//                                sum_m u[m] * dV2D_s[q][m] ]
//
// using the inverse-map Jacobian (Jinv11..Jinv22) and writes the result
// into gradU[elem][var][dim][q]. It is not implemented in this stage: the
// inviscid residual skips it entirely (the convective volume integral does
// not need gradients).
//
// The placeholder below keeps the kernel name registered so that the
// DgField::computeGradient skeleton can be completed later without
// touching the surface/assembly kernels.
